  {
   "legacy_id": "test_academic_engine.AcademicEngineTests.test_changed_same_requirement_id_supersedes_old_contract_and_creates_new_criteria",
   "disposition": "moved",
   "new_ids": [
    "sim.test_academic_requirement_changes.AcademicRequirementChangeTests.test_changed_same_requirement_id_supersedes_old_contract_and_creates_new_criteria",
    "sim.test_academic_requirement_changes.RequirementChangeByGovernanceRuleTests.test_changed_same_requirement_id_by_the_governance_rule_supersedes_old_contract",
    "sim.test_academic_requirement_changes.AcademicOnlyCharterControlTests.test_an_academic_only_charter_control_keeps_the_solved_goal_and_its_basis"
   ],
   "note": "Two versions (A28). The public-control version (sim.test_academic_requirement_changes.AcademicRequirementChangeTests.test_changed_same_requirement_id_supersedes_old_contract_and_creates_new_criteria) replaces the legacy test: it sends the requirement change through the public control as the legacy send_control did, on a goal the configured goal auditors solved on a reviewed theorem instead of a patched _solution_basis, and carries @known_defect('KD-1200'); with the mark removed it fails at the assertion, added right after the accepted control, that the goal is still solved ('unsolved' != 'mathematically_solved'), and under a probe that repairs only the judgment-revision comparison it passes whole. The governance-rule version (sim.test_academic_requirement_changes.RequirementChangeByGovernanceRuleTests.test_changed_same_requirement_id_by_the_governance_rule_supersedes_old_contract) is an added test: it applies the same change by the governance rule alone (academic_scenes.decide_requirements), a transient start state the product does not reach through the public path while KD-1200 is open, and guards the academic follow-up with the legacy assertions until the defect is closed. Stage 2 KD-1200 is now repaired: both public-control and direct-rule versions refresh owner readiness and preserve the mathematical goal on an academic-only change. The historical failure above is retained; current tests have no expected-failure mark."
  },
